From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:51:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PVE backup: pbs: process chunks in parallel

For each chunk of data it reads, the backup job calls a dump callback,
which writes the chunk either to a VMA archive or, through the
proxmox-backup-qemu library, to a Proxmox Backup Server. The job can
have up to max-workers such writes in flight at once, 16 by default.

The VMA writer is not thread safe, so the VMA callback holds the dump
callback mutex while writing. But the PBS callback took that mutex as
well and held it while the library hashes, compresses and encrypts a
chunk and hands it to the HTTP/2 stream. So only one chunk got
processed at a time, independent of max-workers and of the four
threads of the library's runtime.

Stop taking the mutex in the PBS callback, as the library supports
concurrent writes: the index records each chunk at its offset, its
shared state has its own locks, and pending writes fail once the
backup gets aborted. The check for a failed or canceled backup stays,
so that callbacks after that still skip the write.

Backing up 12 GiB of /usr content in stop mode to a PBS on the same
host, an EPYC 9135 with the datastore on NVMe, two runs each with and
without encryption (which made no significant difference):

                       before      after
  time                 26-27 s     8-9 s
  library CPU usage    1 core      3.5-4 cores
  QEMU peak RSS        140 MiB     190-300 MiB

With max-workers set to 1, both took 30 s, with the library using less
than one core and QEMU peaking at about 80 MiB. So that setting can
limit the impact on the host where a faster backup is not worth it.

Against a remote PBS over 10G, the disk got read at 870-930 MiB/s
instead of 530-560 MiB/s, but the total time stayed the same, as that
PBS datastore could not take more.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Link: https://lore.proxmox.com/pve-devel/20261111003918.452105-1-t.lamprecht@proxmox.com/
---
 pve-backup.c | 6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pve-backup.c b/pve-backup.c
index d20c8e39d0..bbe98e045a 100644
--- a/pve-backup.c
+++ b/pve-backup.c
@@ -156,11 +156,7 @@ pvebackup_co_dump_pbs_cb(
 
     bool is_zero_block = size == di->block_size && buffer_is_zero(buf, size);
 
-    qemu_co_mutex_lock(&backup_state.dump_callback_mutex);
-
-    // avoid deadlock if job is cancelled
     if (pvebackup_error_or_canceled()) {
-        qemu_co_mutex_unlock(&backup_state.dump_callback_mutex);
         return -1;
     }
 
@@ -177,14 +173,12 @@ pvebackup_co_dump_pbs_cb(
 
         if (pbs_res < 0) {
             pvebackup_propagate_error(local_err);
-            qemu_co_mutex_unlock(&backup_state.dump_callback_mutex);
             return pbs_res;
         }
 
         reused += pbs_res == 0 ? to_transfer : 0;
     }
 
-    qemu_co_mutex_unlock(&backup_state.dump_callback_mutex);
     pvebackup_add_transferred_bytes(size, is_zero_block ? size : 0, reused);
 
     return size;
